{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/non_tail_recursion_2.march","start_line":12,"start_col":31,"end_line":12,"end_col":45,"message":"Warning: function `sink_all` is structurally recursive but not tail-recursive. If the recursive call is the direct argument of a constructor in tail position, tail-recursion-modulo-cons compiles it to a loop with no extra stack (it always runs). Otherwise it uses O(depth) stack space and deep input can overflow the stack — consider an accumulator parameter.","code":"non_tail_recursion","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/non_tail_recursion_2.march","start_line":15,"start_col":21,"end_line":15,"end_col":23,"message":"`ys` has type `List(b)`, which holds a type variable that a `linear` parameter of `f` opts in to linear values, so a caller may pass a linear value here too.  Mark it `linear ys` (or `affine ys`) so the body is checked to use it once.","code":"linear_generic_param","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
